    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2003-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring gives \\[\\dfrac{2(1-2+3-4+5-6+7)}{3(1-2+3-4+5-6+7)}.\\] The identical alternating sums cancel, leaving \\(\\dfrac{2}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor a \\(2\\) out of the numerator and a \\(3\\) out of the denominator",
        "Both share the factor \\(1-2+3-4+5-6+7\\)"
      ],
